  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1228 PM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nIf you like high temperatures at or over 100 degrees once again, \nyou will enjoy the next several days where most of the Panhandles \nshould experience these temperatures. The main H500 high pressure \nsystem will slowly traverse towards the Four Corners Region by the\nend of the week bringing large scale subsidence to the region. \nSome of the latest global model guidance shows a set up of mid \nlevel NW flow bring rain chances for the northern Panhandles, but \nwe will watch those trends closely as we get later in the week.\nUnfortunately, we will be adding more 100 degree days to the\nsummer for this forecast period, adding to well above average\ntemperatures continuing for mid to late August.",
